<h1>Lego Set Tracker</h1>

<div class="introduction">
	<section class="description">
		<h3>What is this?</h3>
		<p>Lego Set Tracker is a desktop application that helps you manage and rebuild Lego sets from a collection of
			mixed pieces. Whether you have a bin full of loose Lego pieces or multiple sets disassembled, this tool helps
			you track what pieces you need to find and what you already have.</p>
	</section>

	<section class="how-to-use">
		<h3>How to use</h3>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Home:</strong> View this welcome page and overview of the app</li>
			<li><strong>Sets:</strong> Browse, add, and manage your Lego set collection
				<ul>
					<li>Use the search form to find sets by name, set number, or theme</li>
					<li>When viewing a set's pieces, you'll see detailed information for each piece:
						<ul>
							<li>Image of the piece, Amount found, Amount left to find, Amount needed, Name of the piece,
								BrickLink ID, Color, Category</li>
						</ul>
					</li>
					<li>When viewing a set's pieces, you'll see visual indicators showing your progress:
						<ul>
							<li><strong class="danger">Red X</strong> - You found 0 of this piece</li>
							<li><strong class="warning">Yellow X</strong> - You found some of this piece</li>
							<li><strong class="success">Green Checkmark</strong> - You have the exact amount needed</li>
							<li><strong class="info">Blue Plus</strong> - You have extra pieces</li>
						</ul>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li><strong>Settings:</strong> Customize the application theme and preferences</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="features">
		<h3>Features</h3>
		<ul>
			<li>Track all your Lego sets in one place</li>
			<li>View detailed information about each set, including required pieces</li>
			<li>Analyze your collection statistics</li>
			<li>Switch between light, dark, and system themes</li>
			<li>Helps you find the pieces you need to rebuild specific sets</li>
		</ul>
	</section>
</div>
